# A rival company at a discovered site (GenStep_TSC_RivalCompany, wired
# through the same parley component as the crypt looters). They got here
# first, they are not hostile, and every exit resolves the group:
# parley_flee = they ride off the claim; parley_hostile = it comes to
# steel. Paying them off costs real silver (take_item), gated so the
# option cannot fire short. One meeting per group (TSC_WildRivalsMet).

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_WildRivals

== start ==
Riders, and not bandits: road gear, guild-cut cloaks with no charter mark, picks and rope on the saddles. A crew working for themselves. Their leader stands up from the fire and does not reach for anything.

"Well," she says. "The roads are getting crowded. We found this place first, friend, and we mean to work it. There's nothing here worth anyone bleeding over - so let's agree you rode on."

* "The Wayfarers' charter says found claims go to chartered companies. You know the custom. Ride on."
    check Persuasion 9 -> yields | stands
    on success do parley_flee()
* "We'll buy the claim. A hundred and fifty, silver, and you ride out ahead of the weather." -> bought
    if has_item(Silver, 150)
    do take_item(Silver, 150)
    do parley_flee()
* "It's ours now. Count your blades and count ours." -> fight
    do parley_hostile()
* [Leave them to their find and ride on.] -> end

== yields ==
She looks at your company a long moment: the arms, the horses, the charter mark you carry openly.

"Custom," she says, the way people say words they are losing an argument to. "One day the guild's paper is going to write a cheque its riders can't cash. Not today, though." She whistles her crew up. "It's yours. Mind the low gallery."

* [Watch them ride out.] -> end

== stands ==
"Custom cuts both ways, friend. Finders keep, that's the older custom." She sits back down without hurry. "We're not moving. You can share the country or you can make a thing of it."

* "We'll buy the claim. A hundred and fifty, silver." -> bought
    if has_item(Silver, 150)
    do take_item(Silver, 150)
    do parley_flee()
* "Then we make a thing of it." -> fight
    do parley_hostile()
* [Let it go. Ride on.] -> end

== bought ==
She weighs the coin without counting it. That is its own kind of counting.

"Pleasure doing business with the chartered classes." She stands, whistles her crew up, and within the quarter hour theirs is a line of dust on the road. The claim is yours, paid for.

* [To work, then.] -> end

== fight ==
"Ah," she says, and there is real regret in it. "That's a poor trade for everyone." Then the fire is kicked out and the steel is out and the argument has changed languages.

* [Steel.] -> end
